# Documentation

Document what a future contributor (or future you) needs to run, change, or understand the project.

- Keep the root `README.md` accurate for purpose, setup, and conventions
- When adding Cursor rules, update `.cursor/rules/README.md`
- Prefer short, actionable docs over long essays
- Document non-obvious decisions (why), not only mechanics (what)
- If a change alters setup, workflow, or public behavior, update the related docs in the same change

```text
# ❌ BAD
Ship a new workflow rule and leave README stale

# ✅ GOOD
Add the rule and mention it in README / .cursor/rules/README.md
```
